<p>Oh well.  I tried adjusting the temperature, but no go.  I guess I could run the query several times and aggregate the results, but it&#8217;s already pretty slow&#8230;</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-12.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-12.jpeg" alt="" width="621" height="285" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112268" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-12.jpeg 621w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-12-300x138.jpeg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 621px) 100vw, 621px" /></a></p>
<p>After using this for a handful of authors, I&#8217;m now deep in debt.  OK, perhaps not from the API usage, but because I&#8217;ve bought, like, fifteen books while just testing things out here&#8230;</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="625" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112249" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5.jpeg 1927w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5-300x223.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5-1024x763.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5-768x572.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-5-1536x1144.jpeg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I&#8217;ve added convenient commands to the search buffer to go to <tt>bookshop.org</tt> so that I can shop, as well as Goodreads to check whether the books actually exist.  (They mostly do, but there are of course some hallucinations.)</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-13.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-13.jpeg" alt="" width="542" height="134" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112271" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-13.jpeg 542w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-17-13-300x74.jpeg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 542px) 100vw, 542px" /></a></p>
<p>And now I can also do that thing I wanted where there are certain authors that I track, and then query Perplexity for books they&#8217;ve released the last few years.  Let&#8217;s see, I&#8217;ve marked a few authors, and:</p>
