<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-20-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-20-2.jpeg" alt="" width="807" height="64" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112331" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-20-2.jpeg 807w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-20-2-300x24.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-20-2-768x61.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 807px) 100vw, 807px" /></a></p>
<p>Here&#8217;s OpenAI (gpt-4o).</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve put all the query stuff in <tt>query-assistant.el</tt> on <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/bookiez.el" data-cached-time="2025-04-20T18:53:54" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/cache-2025-04-20-web-1.webp" onmouseenter="hoverLink(event)">Microsoft Github</a>.  I didn&#8217;t really expect them to be better &#8212; and they aren&#8217;t &#8212; so no big surprises there.</p>
